The linker error indicates that the device driver for the DAC emulator instances is not being linked into the final binary. This typically happens when the Zephyr build system does not detect any enabled instances of the corresponding device in the device tree.

The node names in `native_sim.overlay` (`dac-emulator-0`, `dac-emulator-1`, `dac-emulator-many`) do not follow the standard `name@address` convention. The build system's scripts, which parse the device tree to identify driver instances, are likely failing to recognize these nodes correctly, especially the `dac-emulator-many` node.

The fix is to rename the nodes to follow the standard convention, such as `dac-emulator@0`, `dac-emulator@1`, and `dac-emulator@2`. This ensures that the build system correctly identifies them as instances of the `zephyr,dac-emulator` compatible, links the driver, and resolves the undefined reference errors. The labels are preserved, so no changes are needed in the C source code.

